#: includes/class-mwwpf-admin-notice.php:90
msgid "The storage for uploaded files can be accessed from outside: a test file placed there was readable over HTTP. Set MWWPF_STORAGE_DIR in wp-config.php to a path outside the document root, or deny access to the storage in the web server configuration."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mwwpf-admin-notice.php:92
msgid "The storage for uploaded files is inside the public directory, and this server does not apply .htaccess protection. Set MWWPF_STORAGE_DIR in wp-config.php to a path outside the document root, or deny access to the storage in the Nginx configuration."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mwwpf-admin-notice.php:101
msgid "The path in MWWPF_STORAGE_DIR cannot be used: it must be an absolute path, and must not be a WordPress directory (such as wp-content or uploads) or a parent of one. The default location is used instead."
msgstr ""

